    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "Does this skill change repository files?",
        "answer": "No. It reads guides and configuration files, then reports extracted standards."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which tools can it recognize?",
        "answer": "It covers EditorConfig, Prettier, ESLint, Ruff, Black, isort, pre-commit, Husky, and common CI checks."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can it work without CONTRIBUTING.md?",
        "answer": "Yes. It can still summarize formatter, linter, hook, and CI rules from configuration files."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does it guarantee every rule is complete?",
        "answer": "No. It reports evidence found in files and should mark missing or ambiguous rules clearly."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can Claude Code or Codex use the result?",
        "answer": "Yes. The summary can guide Claude, Codex, and Claude Code during repository edits."
